{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":592709,"duration_api_ms":588188,"num_turns":27,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4e56048d-93bb-400d-92ba-30188e689ce7","total_cost_usd":2.26681745,"usage":{"input_tokens":15790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":110693,"cache_read_input_tokens":1668498,"output_tokens":19542,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":110693,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":15790,"outputTokens":19542,"cacheReadInputTokens":1668498,"cacheCreationInputTokens":110693,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.09358025,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":60,"outputTokens":8886,"cacheReadInputTokens":619722,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53420,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.1732372,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `enforce_invariants` (invariants.rs), the function applies clamping mutations (pH, indices, DO) to `&mut TankState` before reaching later validation checks (`check_unit_interval`, `check_sum_close_to_one`, `check_non_negative` for reserve_g). If a later check returns `Err`, the state has already been partially mutated by earlier clamps. The new tests in validation.rs (lines 92-127) assert `engine.full_state() == &expected` after an error, which only holds because `TankState::new()` currently produces a state where all clamp operations are no-ops. Fix: either (a) move all pure validation checks before any clamping mutations so errors are returned on unmodified state, or (b) remove the post-error state-equality assertions from tests since they encode a fragile assumption.","rationale":"Non-atomic error handling in enforce_invariants creates a class of subtle bugs: any future change to TankState::new() defaults (e.g., a pH outside [5.5, 8.5]) would cause the validation.rs tests to fail with a confusing state-mismatch error rather than the expected InvariantViolation. More importantly, callers of step_hours that catch errors may observe partially-clamped state, which violates the principle of least surprise for error recovery paths."}],"summary":"Reviewed the per-tick mass budget tracking implementation (tanksim-6e5.1.2.1). The BudgetLedger, total_nitrogen/total_carbon helpers, per-stage snapshot tracking, and closed-system conservation guard are well-designed and comprehensive. All 18 budget_tracking tests pass, including N/C conservation over 24-tick runs, water-change export tracking, shrimp mortality/reproduction conservation, trim-plants conservation, and structural coverage of all element-bearing fields. The zero-cost-when-disabled behavior is confirmed (Option check only, no snapshot allocations). The new invariant checks for shrimp routing parameters (unit interval, partition sum) and reserve_g non-negativity are correct. Documentation in ROUTING.md and scientific_inventory.md is consistent with code. The only failing test (hatch_produces_juveniles) is a pre-existing issue confirmed by testing at prior commits. One non-trivial robustness concern found regarding partial state mutation on error paths in enforce_invariants."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"a72966d1-8e48-4afc-833d-f7493d73300e"}
